  "summary": "**Batch 1 of 1.** The verifier logic looks fine, and the test fixtures match the assertions. The cleanup of the translations has three content errors. The Lithuanian account and login TOTP strings are Italian. The zh_CN account string is Traditional Chinese. The JS apps' `error-invalid-multivalued-size` messages were switched from i18next `{{n}}` to `{n}` with `choice` syntax. That probably breaks them in the account and admin UIs. I did not run anything.\n\n**Batch 1 of 1, retry.** I found no issues in this part. The changes fix broken HTML in the translations: stray `LT` text, a missing `>`, spaces inside tags, and `<br/>` changed to `<br />`. They also drop the FreeOTP and Google Play links from the totp step 1 strings. The Slovak `error-invalid-multivalued-size` now uses `{2,choice,...}` for the max count instead of repeating `{1}`, which fixes a plural bug. The new test fixtures match the assertions in `VerifyMessagePropertiesTest`. `duplicateKeys_en.properties` really does contain `key=value` twice. I only read the test class and `duplicateKeys_en.properties` in full. I judged the other files from the diff, without opening them or checking the surrounding lines.",
